{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And HaShem said, etc.</b> One needs to know why it changed to say here <b>וַיֹּאמֶר</b> [\"and He said\"]. And I saw in the Mekhilta that they said: ״וַיֹּאמֶר ה׳ לְמֹשֶׁה לֵּאמֹר״ [\"And HaShem said to Moses, saying\"] — not by means of an angel and not by means of an emissary. And one needs to know what is different about this verse that they expound it thus, for it would have been more fitting to say these things regarding the ״וַיְדַבֵּר״ [\"and He spoke\"] that is stated first in the Torah. And perhaps they sensed our difficulty and said that ״וַיֹּאמֶר״ is an expression of elevation, in the manner of what He said (Isaiah 3:10): ״אִמְרוּ צַדִּיק כִּי טוֹב״ [\"Say of the righteous that it is good\"], and what is the elevation? — that HaShem spoke to him without an intermediary. And nearby the reason will be explained in another manner."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:34:54.303072673Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}